findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config loading tests don't distinguish NotFound from parse/permission errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Dev implemented InternalDetail wrapper type that suppresses sensitive
    info in Display (CWE-209). Reviewer verified: ''CliError::Display does not leak
    InternalDetail strings to user-facing output.'' However, reviewer also flagged
    ServerError variant leaking response body via source(), so partial catch.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "Dev strips CR/LF from tenant IDs (header injection prevention) but still\
    \ uses raw String, not Option<TenantId> from axiathon-core. The type-safety gap\
    \ \u2014 bypassing validated TenantId \u2014 was not flagged by any phase."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer verified 'All workspace dependencies properly declared' but did
    not flag that 6 deps use direct version strings instead of workspace = true.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: ''RawConfig uses serde::Deserialize without
    #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]. A config file with typos like api_rul or timeoat
    will silently use defaults.'''
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...). TEA wrote config tests but this specific logical flaw was not flagged.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the test with zero assertions that only checks non-panic
    via let _ = config.
